<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 2.4 · Lunar, Cooking & Recipe for Disaster" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="2-4" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 2.4</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Lunar, Cooking & Recipe for Disaster</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Finish useful Fremennik and Lunar infrastructure, make a real food stock while training Cooking, and close the five remaining council members. This is a quest-and-food chapter, not an early 72-Mining or 68-Agility grind.</p>
      </header>

      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Complete The Fremennik Isles, Lunar Diplomacy, One Small Favour and Swan Song; reach actual 60 Mining and actual 70 Cooking; free the five council members Chapter 1 left frozen; defeat the Culinaromancer and buy Barrows gloves."
        stats={["Actual 60 Mining for Lunar (unboostable)", "Actual 65 Magic already guaranteed by 1,590 High Alchs", "Actual 62 Cooking before Swan Song; actual 70 before Awowogei", "181 guaranteed QP at entry; 202 on completion"]}
        unlocks={["Helm of Neitiznot, Lunar spellbook and Piscatoris", "Karambwan fishing/cooking and a permanent food loop", "Full Recipe for Disaster and Barrows gloves", "Two 10,000-XP Herblore lamps; final 20,000-XP lamp reserved for Herblore"]}
      />

      <div class="callout"><strong>Continuity check:</strong> Chapter 1.3 already finished the RFD introduction, Goblin generals, Mountain Dwarf and Pirate Pete. Chapter 2.3 finished Alfred Grimhand's Barcrawl and Horror from the Deep. The exact mandatory route has <strong>181 Quest Points entering this page</strong>: the 107-point Legends' Quest start gate was crossed when The Giant Dwarf took the total from 106 to 108 in 1.3, and Throne of Miscellania took 174 to 175 at the start of 2.3. No optional quests, miniquests or partly started quests are counted. Check your live quest log if you diverged from the route.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Fremennik and Lunar infrastructure</div><h2>Finish the real gates, not a giant skilling detour.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i24-isles" number="1" title="Complete The Fremennik Isles">
        <p><strong>Why now:</strong> The Fremennik Trials, 70 Woodcutting and 50+ Construction are already in place. The quest adds Neitiznot travel and the <strong>Helm of Neitiznot</strong>, a durable melee helm with a Prayer bonus. Take the Rellekka boat to Neitiznot, speak with Mawnis Burowgar and work through the Jatizso/Neitiznot errands as one quest. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Fremennik_Isles" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki quest walkthrough</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Ironman preflight:</strong> bank <strong>nine ropes</strong> (eight if you already own the required shield), an axe, knife, <strong>hammer and bronze nail</strong>, needle and two thread, coins, food and teleports. Bring or make a <strong>Neitiznot shield</strong>: two arctic-pine logs, one rope and the bronze nail/hammer, not a shield bought from another player. Cut <strong>eight more arctic-pine logs and split them</strong> for bridge repair (56 Woodcutting required, already met), and make the yak-hide top and legs from local hides if not banked (46 Crafting, already met). Keep the shield for the troll section. The optional mine shortcut is not a 40-Agility gate for our route.</p>
        <p>Rebank before the <strong>Ice Troll King</strong> (level 122): shield, food, prayer restore and solid melee gear are more important than rushing the final corridor. Kill <strong>ten frenzied ice trolls</strong> with the honour guards first; you can leave and restock before crossing to the king. His Magic/Ranged defence makes melee the practical default; the shield helps with troll ranged damage. Use <strong>Protect from Magic</strong> against the king and <strong>do not use Protect from Melee</strong>, which triggers his knockback attack. Check the live fight guide if unfamiliar. Claim the helm and two <strong>10,000-XP choices among Attack, Strength, Defence or Hitpoints</strong> when finished; put them into whichever later combat gate is actually lagging, then record the live levels. Keep the helm rather than treating it as a disposable quest prop.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-mining-60" number="2" title="Train Mining from actual 50 to actual 60">
        <p><strong>This is a hard Lunar Diplomacy gate:</strong> 60 Mining is not boostable. Read your live level after 2.2; train only the remainder and stop at <strong>actual 60</strong>. No ore quota or 72-Mining checkpoint is hidden here.</p>
        <p><strong>Shooting Stars</strong> are the low-attention choice: locate a landed star via the in-game/world-tracking community, bring a pickaxe, mine a tier your level permits and move to the next star when it depletes. The 2,000 stardust Chapter 1 set aside already bought the celestial ring; any new dust is a bonus. <strong>Motherlode Mine</strong> is the resource-minded choice: mine pay-dirt, deposit it in the hopper, collect ore from the sack and bank it for later Smithing. It asks for more movement but turns this level gate into useful metal stock. If you independently unlocked Cam Torum, calcified deposits are another relaxed option; do not complete Perilous Moons just to enter them. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Pay-to-play_Mining_training" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki Mining methods</a>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i24-mining-methods" informational={true} skill="Mining" target="actual 60" why="Lunar's Mining gate is unboostable; 72 for Making Friends belongs in 2.6." recommended="Shooting Stars for long low-attention sessions, stopping when the skill tab reads 60." resource="Motherlode Mine pay-dirt for ore that later supports Smithing." relaxed="Calcified deposits only if Cam Torum is already unlocked independently." />
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-lunar" number="3" title="Verify actual 65 Magic and complete Lunar Diplomacy">
        <p><strong>Level audit:</strong> Lunar needs unboosted <strong>5 Herblore, 61 Crafting, 40 Defence, 49 Firemaking, 65 Magic, 60 Mining and 55 Woodcutting</strong>, plus The Fremennik Trials, Lost City, Rune Mysteries and Shilo Village. The new Mining checkpoint closes the only intentional skill gap. The mandatory 1,590 High Alchs in 2.1 award <strong>103,350 Magic XP</strong>; even from the Chapter 1 actual-63 floor (368,599 XP), that exceeds level 65's 449,428 XP threshold. The 2.2 mandatory Defence quest rewards and Daero's selected 35,000 Defence XP likewise clear 40 without optional melee training. Verify both levels in the skill tab before departure.</p>
        <p><strong>Consolidated preflight:</strong> bring a pickaxe, axe, hammer, tinderbox, spade, needle and thread, pestle and mortar, a working bullseye lantern (the banked sapphire lantern from Tears of Guthix works), guam and marrentill, roughly 1,000 coins, a <strong>dramen staff</strong>, food and combat supplies. Bring access to the <strong>air, fire, water and earth altars</strong> via talismans/tiaras or the Abyss unlocked by Enter the Abyss. Bank space for the nine Lunar equipment pieces. Ask Brundt for a <strong>seal of passage</strong> and wear it on Lunar Isle or its inhabitants will send you away. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Lunar_Diplomacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki item list and dialogue/puzzle details</a>.</p>
        <p>The long quest builds its own equipment set: turn a dramen staff into a Lunar staff by taking it to the four elemental altars in order, mine/smith Lunar ore for the helm, kill <strong>level-111 Suqahs</strong> for a tooth and four hides, have the hides tanned and sew the garments, and recover the ring, amulet and other pieces through the island tasks. Rebank before Suqahs with antipoison, food and a suitable combat style. Wear <strong>all nine Lunar pieces</strong> to enter Dream World. There, complete the trials and final fight; regular armour, weapons, staves and potions are disallowed, but food and runes are permitted. If you leave, prepare new kindling to return. The Wiki is useful for the trial order rather than guessing dialogue.</p>
        <p>Finish for the <strong>Lunar spellbook</strong>, Lunar Isle/astral access, 50 astral runes and quest XP. Lunar is a second spellbook with travel/support spells; it does not erase the standard spellbook. The earlier High Alchemy block correctly needed standard spells, but do not start a large Lunar-rune production routine here. Keep the seal/staff accessible for later island travel.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Useful quest spine</div><h2>Close RFD requirements while adding future-ready unlocks.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i24-chompy" number="4" title="Complete Big Chompy Bird Hunting and keep its gear">
        <p>This is required for both the <strong>Lumbridge Guide</strong> and <strong>Skrach Uglogwee</strong> RFD chapters. Reach <strong>Rantz</strong> in the eastern Feldip Hills (fairy ring <strong>AKS</strong> nearby). Bring an axe, knife, chisel, feathers, food and a few wolf bones; the quest teaches you to make ogre-arrow shafts from achey logs, tips from wolf bones and then ogre arrows, and gives you an <strong>ogre bow</strong>. Follow Rantz's family story and cook the quest bird on his spit. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Big_Chompy_Bird_Hunting" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki quest walkthrough</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>The unusual hunting loop:</strong> take <strong>ogre bellows</strong> from the chest in Rantz's cave, fill them from the nearby <strong>swamp bubbles</strong>, use them on local swamp toads to make <strong>bloated toads</strong>, then drop those as bait in the hunting area. A chompy may land; shoot it with the ogre bow and ogre arrows. Repeat for the quest's required bird, rather than grinding diary kill counts. Bank the <strong>bellows, ogre bow, arrows and at least one extra raw chompy</strong> for Skrach later.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-murder" number="5" title="Complete Murder Mystery">
        <p>Go to <strong>Sinclair Mansion</strong> north of Seers' Village and speak to the guard. This short evidence quest has no combat or banked-item requirement: collect the dagger, thread, poison and suspect evidence in the mansion, use flour/flypaper for fingerprints, then present the matching case. Keep it as one investigation rather than splicing it into other errands. It supplies <strong>three Quest Points</strong> and closes both the Lumbridge Guide and later King's Ransom prerequisites. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Murder_Mystery" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki evidence walkthrough</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-cold-war" number="6" title="Complete Cold War for the later Weiss quest">
        <p><strong>Why retain it:</strong> Cold War is a prerequisite for <em>Making Friends with My Arm</em>, deliberately scheduled in 2.6, and its one Quest Point is useful progress rather than filler. Talk to <strong>Larry at Ardougne Zoo</strong>. Bring 10 oak planks, 10 steel nails, hammer, spade, a normal plank, silk, a steel bar/clockwork mechanism, raw cod or an activated ring of charos, swamp tar, five ordinary feathers, one mahogany plank and leather; obtain the cowbell during the quest. The 2.1 house can provide the required <strong>crafting table 3</strong>; if you never built one, build it before the clockwork-penguin step. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Cold_War" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki quest details</a>.</p>
        <p>Larry takes you to the iceberg to build a bird hide; watch and record the penguins' greeting emotes. Make the clockwork penguin at your POH crafting table, wear the disguise to infiltrate the colony, gather the cowbell and make the penguin bongos, then clear the ice course and Icelord encounter. Bring some food and do not mistake the penguin course for an optional 68-Agility checkpoint. Finish the quest, but leave Making Friends itself for the later 70s block.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-trio" number="7" title="Complete Tai Bwo Wannai Trio and unlock karambwans">
        <p>This is not an RFD requirement, but the <strong>permanent karambwan food loop</strong> makes it worth doing before Cooking 70. Start with <strong>Timfraku</strong> in Tai Bwo Wannai, then help his three sons around Karamja. Pack an <strong>agility potion (4)</strong> (34 Herblore makes one from toadflax and toad's legs if not banked), an <strong>iron-or-better spear</strong>, small fishing net, knife, pestle and mortar, tinderbox, two logs or an axe, jogre bones, seaweed, a banana and Karamjan rum, plus Magic/Ranged gear for a monkey, antipoison and travel supplies. Jogres can supply the bones and sometimes a spear; if needed, an iron spear is sold at the Fortis Blacksmith. Combine the sliced banana with the rum <strong>before leaving Karamja</strong>. Follow the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Tai_Bwo_Wannai_Trio" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki's item/order details</a> for the odd recipe chain rather than guessing.</p>
        <p><strong>The useful unlock during the quest:</strong> catch stackable <strong>karambwanji</strong> with the small net at the Holy Lake, take 20 to <strong>Lubufu</strong> south-east of Brimhaven, and receive a <strong>karambwan vessel</strong>. Load it with karambwanji; at 65+ Fishing, already guaranteed, fish a raw karambwan on Karamja's north-east coast. For Tamayu, cook one into a <em>poison</em> karambwan and grind it to poison the spear—do not eat it. His hunt then succeeds. Tinsay's burnt-jogre-bone/karambwanji sauce and Tiadeche's vessel/manual errands complete the other two branches. Return to Timfraku, then talk to <strong>Tinsay</strong> in the village to claim the 5,000 Cooking XP and the ability to cook edible karambwans. Keep a vessel for later fishing.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-one-small" number="8" title="Complete One Small Favour; put both lamps into Herblore">
        <p><strong>Why now:</strong> Swan Song needs it, and King's Ransom will need it later. Begin with <strong>Yanni Salika in Shilo Village</strong>, follow his red-mahogany request into the chain of favors, then reverse the chain to deliver the reward. <strong>Bank preflight:</strong> four steel bars, one bronze and one iron bar; two guams, one marrentill and one harralander for Guthix rest; five pigeon cages (available by Jerico's house in East Ardougne); a pot and soft clay for its lid; hammer, chisel, pickaxe, food and teleports. The gem repair uses opal, jade, red topaz and sapphire—bring two cut of each if banked or use a chisel on the quest's uncut gems and replace any crushed ones. Withdraw per region rather than carrying everything all at once. The <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/One_Small_Favour" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">current quest guide</a> has the dialogue/delivery order and bank breaks. This is a long but coherent quest, not a reason to insert unrelated errands at every stop. Make an <strong>extra pot lid</strong> while the recipe is unlocked if you want to reuse it for Swan Song.</p>
        <p>The two selectable lamps give <strong>10,000 XP each</strong> in a skill above 30. Chapter 1's <strong>actual 40 Herblore</strong> qualifies, so use <strong>both on Herblore</strong> and record the resulting live level. That is a guaranteed 20,000 Herblore XP toward the later 50/70 gates, not an assumed level jump from variable passive resources.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-cooking-62" number="9" title="Reach actual 62 Cooking for Swan Song">
        <p>Swan Song asks for 62 Cooking. Tai Bwo Wannai Trio's claimed 5,000 Cooking XP helps, but <strong>does not guarantee the level</strong> from Chapter 1's actual-60 handoff. Cook banked raw fish or begin the karambwan loop below until the skill tab reads <strong>actual 62</strong>. Use a range to reduce burns; the Lumbridge Castle range and cellar chest are already accessible through RFD's introduction. This is the first stop of one Cooking journey, not a separate method-panel checkbox.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-swan" number="10" title="Complete Swan Song and open Piscatoris">
        <p>Check <strong>One Small Favour</strong> above and Chapter 1's <strong>Garden of Tranquillity</strong>, 100+ QP, actual 62 Cooking, 62 Fishing, 45 Smithing, 42 Firemaking and 40 Crafting. Those non-Magic skills are already covered. Swan Song's <strong>66 Magic is boostable</strong>: the mandatory alchs guarantee actual 65, so take a <strong>Wizard's mind bomb (+3 Magic)</strong> for the requirement check rather than grinding a whole Magic level. If your actual Magic has reached 66 from other play, no boost is needed. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Swan_Song" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki quest details</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Preflight:</strong> 10 mist runes, 10 lava runes, five blood runes, a lidded pot (or two soft clay to make pot and lid), five iron bars, logs, tinderbox, hammer, food, prayer restore, combat gear and a small fishing net. Seven bones can be obtained during the quest. Reach the <strong>Piscatoris Fishing Colony</strong> by Kathy Corkat's boat west of Tree Gnome Stronghold (50 coins or ring of charos) or fairy ring <strong>AKQ</strong> and a walk. Help the Wise Old Man defend and repair the colony, bank before the level-170 <strong>Sea Troll Queen</strong>, and use an appropriate ranged or Magic setup with food; she uses multiple styles and drains Prayer. Finish for Piscatoris access and its monkfish fishery, another useful food option. Do not infer any particular Cooking XP from fishing there.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <ExpandableNote label="Optional early unlock" title="Making Friends with My Arm may be done early only if you already meet its gates">
        <p>If you independently have or can comfortably boost <strong>68 Agility and 72 Mining</strong>, have <strong>66 Firemaking and 35 Construction</strong>, and completed Swan Song, Cold War and My Arm's Big Adventure, you may do Making Friends now for the disease-free Weiss herb patch and large XP rewards. It is <strong>not required in 2.4</strong>; 2.6 is its mandatory home alongside the actual-70 Agility/Mining work for Song of the Elves. No 2.4 Quest Point or skill calculation counts this optional early branch. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Making_Friends_with_My_Arm" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki requirements</a>.</p>
      </ExpandableNote>

      <RouteStep id="i24-cooking-70" number="11" title="Build useful food stock and reach actual 70 Cooking">
        <p><strong>Why 70:</strong> King Awowogei's RFD chapter requires it. The game allows a boost, but this route takes <strong>actual 70</strong> so the requirement and a durable food stock are both solved. Check banked raw fish from Tempoross and other play first. Cook those before catching more; fish from ordinary Barbarian Fishing gutting is generally processed for its small Cooking XP rather than a promised raw-fish stock.</p>
        <p><strong>Recommended relaxed loop:</strong> take the retained <strong>karambwan vessel</strong> and stackable <strong>karambwanji bait</strong>. Net more karambwanji at the Holy Lake near Tai Bwo Wannai, bait the vessel, fish raw karambwan at the north-east Karamja shore (fairy ring <strong>DKP</strong> nearby), bank a comfortable batch, then cook normally on a range. Select <strong>cooked/edible karambwan</strong>, not the poison preparation used during the quest. The Hosidius Kitchen offers a nearby bank and reduced burns <em>if</em> you independently completed the Easy Kourend & Kebos diary; do not assume that optional diary. The <strong>Lumbridge Castle range</strong> is the guaranteed low-burn fallback, with the RFD chest in the cellar. Expect burns and fish enough to cover them. No one-tick cooking is assumed. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Ironman_Guide/Cooking" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki Ironman Cooking</a>.</p>
        <p>Already-banked fish or ordinary leaping-fish gutting can fill the gap if you prefer; Fishing is already 74, so further fishing is for enjoyment, food or side XP, <em>not</em> a hidden Fishing gate. A more active cooking activity is optional if you enjoy it, but no click-intensive method is budgeted. Check live Cooking XP after each batch and stop only at <strong>actual 70</strong>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i24-cooking-methods" informational={true} skill="Cooking" target="actual 70" why="Awowogei is the one hard food-skill stop here; produce food rather than chasing an arbitrary catch count." recommended="Normal fish-and-cook karambwan batches after Tai Bwo Wannai Trio, creating a useful PvM food bank." resource="Cook existing Tempoross and other raw fish first at the guaranteed Lumbridge range; use the Hosidius Kitchen only if its diary is already done." relaxed="Ordinary Barbarian Fishing and inventory gutting is a supplementary multi-skill break, not a Fishing requirement or 3-tick cut-eat assumption." />
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Finish the council</div><h2>Five members remain; the first three were freed in Chapter 1.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i24-legends-access" number="12" title="Verify 107 QP and start Legends' Quest for Kharazi access">
        <p><strong>STOP and check Quest Points:</strong> the mandatory route was already <strong>181 QP entering 2.4</strong> and is <strong>196 QP after Swan Song</strong>; the 107-QP gate was crossed in Chapter 1.3. Family Crest, Heroes' Quest, Shilo Village, Underground Pass and the rest of the Legends prerequisite chain are already complete. Bring an axe, machete, <strong>charcoal and at least three papyrus</strong> (bring spares because they can break), jungle supplies/antipoison and travel items to <strong>Radimus Erkle at the Legends' Guild</strong>. Take his notes, enter the Kharazi Jungle south of Shilo Village and use the notes to map the three areas. The route's 70 Woodcutting covers the jungle step. Keep the <strong>Radimus notes</strong> for later entry and collect a <strong>vanilla pod</strong> in the south-west jungle for Sir Amik. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Legends%27_Quest" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki partial-start map instructions</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Stop after access and the vanilla pod.</strong> Full Legends' Quest is not needed to free Sir Amik and its additional 45-Herblore gate is not being smuggled into this chapter. A started quest gives <strong>zero Quest Points</strong> until completed.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-guide" number="13" title="Free the Lumbridge Guide">
        <p>Big Chompy and Murder Mystery are now complete; Biohazard, Demon Slayer, Nature Spirit and Witch's House were finished in Chapter 1. Take a <strong>bucket of milk, egg, pot of flour and cake tin</strong> (or buy them from the Culinaromancer's Chest), inspect the frozen Guide in Lumbridge Castle and visit <strong>Wizard Traiborn</strong> at the Wizards' Tower. He enchants the three ingredients through quest-memory questions and item puzzles; use the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Recipe_for_Disaster/Freeing_the_Lumbridge_Guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki quiz guide</a> when the randomized question needs a reminder. Make/bake the cake of guidance, return it to the Guide and confirm the subquest's one QP.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-evil-dave" number="14" title="Free Evil Dave with a measured spice stew">
        <p>Gertrude's Cat and Shadow of the Storm are already complete. Bring a <strong>grown cat or hellcat</strong> (not an overgrown cat; a kitten catches slowly) and up to <strong>nine ordinary stews</strong>. If your only cat is still a kitten, let it mature while doing the preceding quests or accept a much slower catch rate; do not assume an unmentioned mature cat was guaranteed. Inspect Dave at the table, then go to <strong>Doris's house west of Edgeville bank</strong> and descend into the basement. Tell Dave the magic requires him to describe the stew. Your cat catches <strong>hell-rats</strong>, which drop brown, red, yellow or orange spice shakers. This is a cat-and-recipe puzzle, not combat training. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Recipe_for_Disaster/Freeing_Evil_Dave" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki spice procedure</a>.</p>
        <p>For each colour, test a stew containing <strong>one dose of that colour only</strong>. Dave says whether a spice amount is correct. If not, test two; if neither one nor two works, the needed amount is three. Write down all four results, then combine the exact doses on a final stew. Finish Dave's dialogue and <strong>use</strong> the stew on frozen Dave in Lumbridge; do not eat it. Keep surplus spice only if you want later stew boosts—the route does not depend on them.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-skrach" number="15" title="Free Skrach Uglogwee with a cooked jubbly">
        <p>Retrieve the banked <strong>ogre bellows, ogre bow/arrows, extra raw chompy</strong> and an <strong>iron spit</strong>. Bring an axe, any log, tinderbox, pickaxe and a ball of wool; the quest's 41 Cooking and 20 Firemaking are covered. Inspect Skrach, talk to <strong>Rantz</strong> by Feldip Hills, cut his boat-tree twice, then go to the marked Karamja landing (fairy ring <strong>CKR</strong> is nearby). Cook the raw chompy on the spit/fire by the arrow-marked tree to call the boat, cross, and report back to Rantz. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Recipe_for_Disaster/Freeing_Skrach_Uglogwee" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki boat/jubbly sequence</a>.</p>
        <p>For the jubbly, take a <strong>bloated toad</strong> from Rantz's swamp, a nearby rock and the ball of wool. Use charged bellows on the bloated toad to make a <strong>balloon toad</strong>, drop it as bait and shoot the spawned jubbly with ogre arrows. Spawn/kill again if needed; cook the raw jubbly on Rantz's spit-roast, then use the cooked bird on Skrach in Lumbridge. This is why we preserved the chompy equipment instead of reacquiring it.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-sir-amik" number="16" title="Free Sir Amik Varze; leave Legends only partly done">
        <p>Check your <strong>107+ Quest Points</strong>, started Legends' Quest, Kharazi access and vanilla pod. Inspect Sir Amik and <strong>ask the Lumbridge Cook about him</strong> before visiting the Wise Old Man. Gather a bucket of milk, pot of cream, pot of cornflour (mill raw sweetcorn if needed), vanilla pod, <strong>dramen branch</strong>, pestle and mortar, <strong>ice gloves</strong>, dramen/Lunar staff and an ordinary <strong>raw chicken</strong>. Assemble the crème brûlée ingredients in the Cook's order. If Swan Song dialogue temporarily masks the Wise Old Man's Evil Chicken option, finish Swan Song first—which this route already did. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Recipe_for_Disaster/Freeing_Sir_Amik_Varze" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki ingredient and fight details</a>.</p>
        <p>Ask the Wise Old Man about strange beasts/the Evil Chicken. Bank in <strong>Zanaris</strong>, then enter the Evil Chicken's Lair by using raw chicken on its shrine. Bring an <strong>anti-dragon shield</strong>, food, prayer restore, antipoison as needed and Magic/Ranged supplies. Kill a <strong>level-227 black dragon</strong> for its token—safespots exist—then the Evil Chicken for its egg. Do not treat this as free loot or rely on the optional 65/65/65 melee route. Finish the brûlée with egg and crushed dramen-branch cinnamon; use the token/dragonfire step as the quest directs, with ice gloves, and deliver it to Sir Amik. Full Legends completion remains deferred.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-awowogei" number="17" title="Free King Awowogei at actual 70 Cooking">
        <p>Check <strong>actual 70 Cooking</strong>, 48+ Agility and Chapter 2.2's Monkey Madness I. Inspect Awowogei, take the retained <strong>M'speak amulet and Karamjan monkey greegree</strong> to Ape Atoll, and talk to the <strong>three wise monkeys</strong> in the temple. They explain that a big snake must be stuffed with a <strong>red banana</strong> and <strong>tchiki monkey nuts</strong>, not ordinary banana/nuts. Bring rope, knife, pestle and mortar, food, antipoison and combat gear. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Recipe_for_Disaster/Freeing_King_Awowogei" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki full subquest</a>.</p>
        <p>Make <strong>gorilla, ninja and zombie greegrees</strong> if not already owned: get three blank talismans, the corresponding monkey bones and take them to Zooknock in the Ape Atoll dungeon. Gorilla form reaches the red-banana tree, ninja form traverses the agility course for tchiki nuts, and zombie form crosses the temple's hot coals. On <strong>Crash Island</strong>, kill level-84 big snakes in the pit for corpses; turn on Protect from Melee before entering. Take several corpses and ingredients because the stuffed snake can burn even at 70. Slice banana, grind nuts, stuff the corpses, then cook on the <strong>long hot rock</strong> past the temple coals. Use the successfully cooked snake on Awowogei in Lumbridge while wearing M'speak. Do not eat it.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-final-gate" number="18" title="STOP: verify all council members and 175+ Quest Points">
        <p>Before entering the final portal, open the quest list. The four Chapter 1.3 credits (RFD introduction + Goblin, Dwarf and Pirate), the five members on this page, and the standalone prerequisites must all be complete. This route's guaranteed total is <strong>201 QP before the finale</strong>, already well above the <strong>175-QP</strong> requirement. The total comes from named mandatory quests only; optional Making Friends, full Legends and any miniquest are excluded. If your live total differs, compare it to the ledger's per-quest audit instead of doing random filler.</p>
        <p>Also verify <strong>Desert Treasure I and Horror from the Deep</strong>, both already finished, and prepare a bank of food, restores, <strong>ice gloves</strong>, Magic/Ranged gear and suitable runes. Your real post-2.3 Magic/Ranged and Hitpoints matter more than an assumed optional melee level. You can switch styles and restock between bosses.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i24-culinaromancer" number="19" title="Defeat the Culinaromancer and buy Barrows gloves">
        <p>Enter the Lumbridge Castle dining-room portal after the <strong>175-QP check</strong>. The fights are instanced; <strong>Prayer is disabled</strong>, but you can leave and bank/restock <strong>between individual bosses</strong>. Bring substantial food and play each encounter separately. Agrith-Na-Na, Flambeed, Karamel, Dessourt and the Gelatinnoth Mother do not all favour one style: bring Magic/Ranged options, including an upgraded Iban's staff if your actual Attack/Magic allow it. Wear <strong>ice gloves for Flambeed</strong>; Karamel drains stats, so restores help; the Mother changes vulnerabilities and rewards the elemental/style switches learned in Horror from the Deep. The final Culinaromancer hits hard but has low Defence. Use the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Recipe_for_Disaster/Defeating_the_Culinaromancer" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wiki boss notes</a> for detailed attack cues. There is no invented mandatory melee grind here.</p>
        <p>Completion adds <strong>one Quest Point</strong> for a guaranteed <strong>202-QP exit</strong> and full chest access. Buy <strong>Barrows gloves for 130,000 coins</strong> from the Culinaromancer's Chest in the Lumbridge cellar. They are a strong all-style glove upgrade; put them in your normal combat kit. The final <strong>20,000-XP antique lamp</strong> requires a skill <strong>above 50</strong> and <strong>can be banked</strong>. Prefer Herblore when eligible; if it is still below the lamp threshold, <strong>bank and reserve the lamp for Herblore after 50</strong>. Do not click a different skill just to clear the inventory.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">2.4 exit check</div>
        <h3>A Lunar-capable account with a real food stock and Barrows gloves.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>The Fremennik Isles</strong> complete and Helm of Neitiznot kept; <strong>actual 60 Mining</strong>, Lunar Diplomacy and the Lunar spellbook unlocked.</li>
          <li>Big Chompy, Murder Mystery, Cold War, Tai Bwo Wannai Trio, One Small Favour and Swan Song complete; <strong>both One Small Favour lamps used on Herblore</strong>.</li>
          <li><strong>Actual 70 Cooking</strong> verified, with banked fish/karambwans according to your chosen method; Piscatoris and the karambwan loop open.</li>
          <li><strong>Legends' Quest started and Kharazi Jungle accessible</strong>, but full Legends need not be complete. All five remaining RFD council members and the Culinaromancer finished; <strong>202 guaranteed Quest Points and Barrows gloves owned</strong>.</li>
          <li>Use the RFD 20,000-XP lamp on Herblore only if eligible; otherwise bank it for Herblore after actual 50. <strong>Making Friends with My Arm is deferred to 2.6</strong> unless you voluntarily did it early.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Next, the combat/Piety/Morytania lane can use the new gloves and food. Do not assume optional 65/65/65 melee training, a completed Legends' Quest, or early Making Friends.</p>
      </section>

